{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogNaStokesOrdering","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DilogNaStokesOrdering","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBIteratedLimit","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.DilogPartBEulerTail"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.naStokes_physical_partB_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.naStokes_physical_partB_value","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L100-L117","doc":"**Conditional value of the physical Part-B observable under the na-Stokes ordering.**\n\n*If* the na-Stokes identification holds (`[NaStokesPartBOrdering x]` — the OPEN hypothesis),\n*then* the physical Part-B value is `Li₂ x − π²/3`.\n\nDerived, not projected: `tendsto_nhds_unique` forces `wp1Physical = Li₂ x − π²/6`\n(against the proved `wp1_outer_tendsto`) and `wp2Physical = π²/6` (against the proved\n`QOU.QPochhammer.euler_tail_asymptotic`) by uniqueness of limits, then the additive\nassembly gives `(Li₂ x − π²/6) − π²/6 = Li₂ x − π²/3`.  The `−π²/3` is an *abelian* dilog\ncusp value (two `Li₂(1) = π²/6` boundary terms), **not** a claimed curvature term\n(see the audit cross-referenced in the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.partB_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.partB_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L98-L98","doc":"**Additive assembly** of Part B from its two ordered pieces: bulk minus tail.  Relates\nthree unknowns; carries no closed value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.physicalPartB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.physicalPartB","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The assembled physical Part-B observable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp2_euler_tail_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp2_euler_tail_identification","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L91-L91","doc":"**na-Stokes identification, W-P2 (OPEN).**  The physical W-P2 tail is the `p→1⁻` limit\nof the regularized negative-factor Euler tail (`euler_tail_asymptotic`'s summand); its\nvalue is derived downstream, not asserted here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp2Physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp2Physical","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The physical W-P2 (Euler-tail / Dedekind-eta) contribution — the second unknown. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp1_iterated_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp1_iterated_identification","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L84-L84","doc":"**na-Stokes identification, W-P1 (OPEN).**  The physical W-P1 value is the OUTER\n(`ρ→1⁻`) limit of the proved INNER bulk family `ρ ↦ Li₂ x − Li₂ ρ` (whose pointwise\nvalue is `wp1_bulk_tendsto`, #4343).  The identification of *that iterated limit* with\nthe physical observable is the conjectural input; its numerical value is **not**\nasserted here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp1Physical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.wp1Physical","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The physical W-P1 (bulk) contribution — the unknown the identification pins. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering.mk","kind":"ctor","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L76-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.NaStokesPartBOrdering","kind":"class","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/DilogNaStokesOrdering.lean#L68-L98","doc":"**Na-Stokes path-ordering identification for Dilog Part B (primary conjecture).**\n\nCarries the genuinely-open hypothesis that the physical Part-B observable is the\nτ-shadow of a path-ordered holonomy, hence computed by the **iterated** limit of the two\nregularized scalar sums (W-P1 bulk + W-P2 tail), in the ordered-refinement `(q then ρ)`\norder — never the joint/symmetric limit (illegal on a `𝒫exp`).  The class asserts nothing\nprovable-outright and no instance is fabricated; the value `Li₂ x − π²/3` is **not** a\nfield — it is derived downstream in `naStokes_physical_partB_value`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}